  "result": "I wrote the acceptance tests for spec 001-goals in `app/server/tests/acceptance/001-goals.test.ts`. There are 31 tests covering AC1–AC8, including every value and boundary the spec lists.\n\nI ran `npm --prefix app/server run test:acceptance` and all 31 tests fail, as expected before implementation. They fail because `/api/goals` doesn't exist yet (it returns 404), not because of syntax, import or setup errors.\n\nThe spec had no blocking gaps, so I didn't write `questions.md`. The report in `runs/001-goals/2026-11-22T18-18-51_tester/report.md` has the criterion-to-test table, the run result and six non-blocking spec remarks. The ones that most affect the tests:\n- **Period values:** the API section doesn't say what to send, so the tests assume uppercase `\"WEEKLY\"` / `\"MONTHLY\"`, taken from the data model.\n- **401 responses:** the spec gives no error code, so those tests check only the status and `data: null`.\n- **Undefined cases:** a missing `habitId` and a PUT with an empty body aren't covered by any criterion, so they aren't tested.\n\nRESULT: TESTS_WRITTEN",
